#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:3
msgid "``ci.yaml``: the thresholds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:5
msgid ""
"One file, one name, one syntax, in all three kinds of repository — the "
"engine, a formats repository, an input database. It is committed, it is "
"what the repository owner edits, and it is the only file you have to open"
" to answer \"what does this repository demand of a commit\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:22
msgid ""
"Patterns are shell globs, so ``release/*`` works and a plain name is an "
"exact match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:24
msgid ""
"``package.yaml`` and ``metadata.yaml`` say what a repository *is*. "
"``ci.yaml`` says how it is *gated*, which is a different question with a "
"different audience — and the engine repository, which has no manifest, "
"needs no manifest invented for the purpose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:28
msgid "Two things in the file are **errors**, and deliberately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:30
msgid ""
"a branch matching two class lists. Resolving that silently would make the"
" class of a commit depend on the order of a mapping nobody reads;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:32
msgid ""
"a threshold on a metric this repository cannot measure. A threshold that "
"can never be evaluated is a threshold somebody only thinks they have."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:35
msgid ""
"Absent, everything falls to the defaults: class ``dev``, no thresholds, "
"the default key server — which is to say a repository nobody has "
"configured reports and never refuses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/devops/ci-yaml.rst:40
msgid ""
"``off`` is one of the ten words YAML 1.1 spells a boolean with, so a bare"
" ``off:`` key parses as ``False``. The reader maps it back, so both "
"``off:`` and ``\"off\":`` name the class. You do not have to quote it."
msgstr ""

